"New CR: unique usernames. Sign-up requires a username plus a phone or an email; after verification the person signs in with username and password. Phone and email can be added later in Settings, and a person can be invited by either phone or email. Decisions already made by the user: (1) one sign-in field accepts username, phone or email; (2) username 3-20 characters, Latin letters, digits, underscore and dot, case-insensitive unique, must not look like a phone number or email; Bangla script not allowed; (3) username changeable later, old name held from reuse for a cooling-off period; (4) teachers can record an email as well as a phone for students and guardians, and invitations match on either, re-matching when a person adds a contact later. Constraints identified: dormant teacher-recorded accounts carry no username until claimed, and sign-up on a recorded identifier claims that account; username is owner-private (never in a teacher-lens response, joins the privacy-gate field set); an account keeps at least one verified phone or email and cannot remove its last one; existing activated accounts pick a username at next sign-in while identifier sign-in keeps working; username availability checks and per-username sign-in failures are rate-limited."
